--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY NOTICES & ACADEMIC ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. University Coursework Baseline:
   CookingBroski originated as an academic project for the Conversational Agents
   course at Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam (repository: VU-PCA-2026/agent-2026-am1 ; branch `main`).
   Original team contributors:
   - Mikołaj Duchliński (@ducchuu)
   - Fady Eshak (@fady-eshak)
   - Bennett Hampel (@bugheadwhat)
   - Abdelmatine Daddah (@Abdelmatine24)
   - Kabir D'Souza (@kabirds7)
   - Lazar Gyoshev (@lazargyoshev)

   The original project assets included the Social Interaction Cloud (SIC)
   framework baseline, initial MARBEL dialogue assets, and the Prolog recipe
   knowledge base.

2. Independent Cloud & MLOps Extensions:
   The extensions contained in the `cloud` branch—including the Python dialogue
   manager, pyswip integration, DistilBERT ONNX FP32 intent/slot pipeline,
   dataset curation & CI/CD audit gates, Faster-Whisper local STT cascade,
   Claude Haiku fallback streaming, Google Cloud Run containerization,
   and Cloudflare Tunnel homelab deployment—were independently developed by
   Mikołaj Duchliński and are licensed under the MIT License above.

3. Third-Party Libraries & Models:
   - DistilBERT: Apache 2.0 License (HuggingFace / HuggingFace Transformers)
   - Faster-Whisper / CTranslate2: MIT License / Apache 2.0 License
   - SWI-Prolog: Simplified BSD License (BSD-2-Clause)
   - PySWIP: MIT License
   - Flask & Werkzeug: BSD-3-Clause License

